{title: Count the Stars}
{subtitle: Genesis 15:1–6; 12:1–4; 22:7–8}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
An old man in Haran with [C]his flocks and with his kin
Heard [Bb]a voice that called him out to where [Dm]he'd never been
Leave your land, your kin[C]dred, and your father's house
[Bb]And go to the land I [Dm]will show you
[Bb]So Abram went, as the [C]LORD had told him
With Sa[Bb]rai by his side and the long [C]road in his eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [Dm]years went by in Canaan and the [C]cradle still stood bare
Lord [Bb]GOD, what will you give [Dm]me
I remain childless
[C]He brought him outside
And [Bb]told the childless man to lift his [Dm]weary eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Look up at the sky and [C]count the stars
If you can [Bb]count them
So shall your [Dm]offspring be
Abram believed the LORD
And he [C]credited it to him as [Bb]right[C]eous[Dm]ness
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | [Bb] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Up the mountain walked a fa[C]ther with the son he loved
[Bb]Here are the fire and the [Dm]wood
But where is the lamb
God himself [C]will provide the lamb
And the two [Bb]of them [C]walked on to[Dm]gether
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Look up at the sky and [C]count the stars
If you can [Bb]count them
So shall your [Dm]offspring be
Abram believed the LORD
And he [C]credited it to him [Bb]as [C]righteous[Dm]ness
